---
const elsewhere = [
  { label: 'GitHub', href: 'https://github.com/rizkhal', handle: 'rizkhal' },
  { label: 'X', href: 'https://x.com/rixzkl', handle: '@rixzkl' },
]
---

<section id="about" class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
  <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10">
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <h2 class="text-2xl tracking-tight md:text-3xl">About</h2>

      <div class="mt-6 max-w-[65ch] space-y-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted md:text-base">
        <p>
          I work at Lamaau Labs in Jakarta. Most of what I ship is tooling: a datatable package on
          Packagist, a face-search app that runs entirely offline, a placeholder image service, and a
          pile of small utilities that scratch an itch. The interesting part is rarely the model. It
          is the ingest, the cache, and the one field that arrives as a string on Tuesdays.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything I build runs on infrastructure I can read end to end: Postgres, SQLite, Hono,
          Docker, one VPS, and a reverse proxy. I would rather ship a boring system that survives
          contact with real data than a clever one that needs a babysitter.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-5 lg:pl-10">
      <h3 class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-faint">Elsewhere</h3>
      <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-px bg-line">
        {
          elsewhere.map((item) => (
            <li class="bg-bg">
              <a
                href={item.href}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener me"
                class="group flex items-center justify-between gap-4 py-4"
              >
                <span class="text-sm text-text transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">
                  {item.label}
                </span>
                <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted">{item.handle}</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
